WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.944 --> 00:00:05.088
"Early booking" usually comes up in two different senses.

2
00:00:05.424 --> 00:00:13.824
There's early booking in terms of the date — reserving far ahead of the wedding — and early booking in terms of time, starting earlier than normal working hours on the morning of the wedding.

3
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:21.888
Not many shops offer a discount just for booking a fall wedding as early as spring, so let's focus on the early-time booking that applies on the wedding day itself.

4
00:00:22.224 --> 00:00:25.944
If your appointment starts early in the morning, you'll pay an early fee.

5
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:34.104
Early booking generally refers to the fee charged for starting before the normal 9 a.m. opening time — say, 6 or 7 a.m.

6
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:40.896
For example, for a 6 a.m. start, the makeup or hair artist has to wake up at 4 a.m. to get ready and come in,

7
00:00:41.232 --> 00:00:47.328
so a fee like transportation costs is charged in consideration of that, and it rises a little the earlier you start.

8
00:00:47.664 --> 00:00:51.528
The cutoff time and fee vary by shop, so be sure to check.

9
00:00:51.864 --> 00:00:56.784
It's typically around 30,000 to 50,000 won — roughly the transportation cost for the artist coming in early.
